Because git is GPL-2.0-only, anyone who redistributes these binaries (including the release
archives from this repo) must satisfy the GPL, such as making the corresponding source available
and keeping the GPL notice attached. The release workflow attaches the exact vendored sources
used for the build (git-static-sources.tar.gz) to every release for this purpose.

OpenSSL is vendored under vendor/openssl only for self-built binaries (build.sh --tls openssl)
and is not part of the released archives. Its Apache License 2.0 is considered incompatible with
GPL-2.0-only by the Free Software Foundation, so binaries linking git with OpenSSL should not be
redistributed.
